Package: rav-audio
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: jch.pallier <jch.pallier@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: @SHLIBS@, mpd (>= 0.24), pipewire, pipewire-bin, wireplumber, libspa-0.2-bluetooth, bluez, bluez-tools, systemd
Recommends: fonts-dejavu-core
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Description: SalonRPI audio box: MPD, PipeWire, Bluetooth and dual OLED visualizer
 Turns a Raspberry Pi 3 with two SSD1309 OLEDs into a music player: MPD
 and Bluetooth A2DP play through PipeWire (running as user mpd), and the
 visualizer draws the monitor of the output on the OLEDs. The transport
 buttons drive MPD, or the connected phone over AVRCP.
 .
 Output: an I2S DAC such as a HifiBerry when its overlay is enabled,
 otherwise the onboard headphone jack (dtparam=audio=on). Needs
 dtparam=spi=on for the OLEDs.
